# The #45 conformance corpus is a byte-exact freeze of the v1 on-disk format. The fixtures
# must be checked out byte-for-byte identical on every platform, so git must never apply
# end-of-line (CRLF<->LF) conversion to them. The `.digest` sidecar is text but is compared
# byte-exactly too, so it is pinned the same way. Without this, a Windows checkout under
# core.autocrlf=true would rewrite the `.digest` newline and break the byte gate.
crates/ironbus-core/tests/corpus/*.bin    -text
crates/ironbus-core/tests/corpus/*.digest -text

# The #385 fuzz REGRESSION corpus is content-addressed: each file's name is the SHA-256 of its
# own raw bytes. Any CRLF<->LF rewrite would change the bytes and break the name<->content
# invariant the replay test checks, so these raw seed files must never be EOL-converted either.
fuzz/corpus-regression/** -text
